  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Capacity Development Programme - ZARDD (Caritas Zomba, Malawi)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The quality and speed of CAFOD&#x2019;s humanitarian work depends on the strength of its partners and as part of the Humanitarian Capacity Development Programme, this project aims to strengthen ZARDD&apos;s capacity to prepare, plan and deliver effective humanitarian programmes in Malawi.

The management of large-scale emergency programmes by these local organisations such as Zomba Research and Development Department (ZARDD) places a great strain on their staff and systems. ZARDD, frequently has a much wider remit than emergency work and many of its staff and volunteers have little or no humanitarian experience. There is therefore a need for much greater investment to develop and reinforce permanent local capacity to prepare for and respond to emergencies.

The three core areas of capacity that ZARDD will be assessed against and supported are: Leadership, Skills &amp; Knowledge, as well as Systems &amp; Support Sectors. ZARDD has prioritised, Emergency Preparedness, Accountability, Design &amp; Response, Monitoring, Evaluation and Learning, as well as fundraising  as areas of high priority in having their capacity developed/enhanced.</narrative>
  </description>
